    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello,</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m using plyr 1.8.1. I&#39;m having trouble retaining list names when using alply followed by ldply. Here&#39;s a simple case:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> foo </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;a&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> bar </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mlply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">foo</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># why aren&#39;t the names from foo?</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> foo </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># ok, set them anyways</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;a&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ldply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># uses the old list names?</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> X1 V1<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ldply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">id</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;name&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># ignores the .id param?</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> X1 V1<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>If I look at `bar`, the names are changed, but `split_levels` are not, which I assume is the reason.</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> bar<br>$a<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>$b<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>attr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;split_type&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;array&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>attr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;split_labels&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  X1<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Is this expected behavior? If so, how can I get around it?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you!</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
