     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Kenneth, </div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m not sure if the behaviour is expected, but I&#39;m confused by your first chunk because</div><div><font face=\"monospace\"><br></font></div><div><div><font face=\"monospace\">&gt; library(plyr)</font></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><font face=\"monospace\">&gt; foo &lt;- c(&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;)</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace\">&gt;  bar &lt;- mlply(foo, function(x) 1)</font></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><font face=\"monospace\">&gt; names(foo)</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace\">NULL</font></div></div><div><br></div><div>So foo here is not a named object to begin with! But, I see if we name foo, bar still doesn&#39;t have the names. However, the ldply calls seem to work with the names. In this case split_labels have the names, even though names(bar) doesn&#39;t behave as you expect: </div><div><font face=\"monospace\"><br></font></div><div><div><font face=\"monospace\">&gt; library(plyr)</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace\">&gt; foo &lt;- list(a=&quot;a&quot;, b= &quot;b&quot;)</font></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><font face=\"monospace\">&gt;  bar &lt;- mlply(foo, function(x) 1)</font></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><font face=\"monospace\">&gt; names(foo)</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace\">[1] &quot;a&quot; &quot;b&quot;</font></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><font face=\"monospace\">&gt; names(bar) # why aren&#39;t the names from foo?</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace\">[1] &quot;1&quot; &quot;2&quot;</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace\">&gt; names(bar) &lt;- foo # ok, set them anyway</font></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
